 "title": "Flat states exist on the whole knot sphere: each corner twists labels by -1",
 "subject": "Whether single-vortex label (flat) states exist on the whole octahedral knot sphere, where the lattice's three-colour structure is twisted at the six corners",
 "conclusion": "Sublattice-and-sign frames on the octahedral knot sphere are flat except at the six corners, each of which twists labels by exactly -1. So for every point z and every six disjoint cuts from z to the corners, one constant label developed over the cut sphere violates exactly one line, through z, and the vortex moves by local re-routing.",
